            <ArticleTitle>Gastrointestinal problems in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastrointestinal problems in the elderly, such as swallowing difficulties, chest pain, bleeding, constipation, and colonic diseases, which may present problems in diagnosis or management, are discussed. A screening procedure for colorectal cancer in asymptomatic geriatric patients is proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
